        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(backup): filter agent volatile dirs, browser cache, and lock files from archives",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nBackup archive creation includes volatile runtime paths under agent homes and browser user-data directories. These paths are large, short-lived, and race-prone — when a volatile file disappears during tar creation, backup can fail.\n\nCloses #98865\n\n## Fix\n\nExtend `isVolatileBackupPath` to exclude:\n- Agent runtime `tmp`, `.tmp`, `cache`, `shell_snapshots` under `agents/<id>/agent/`\n- Browser cache paths under `browser/`\n- Retired archive paths under `archived/`\n- Lock, partial, journal, WAL, and SHM files\n\n**2 files, +65 lines**\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Real behavior proof — production function call\n\n```\nnode --import tsx -e \"import { isVolatileBackupPath } from ./src/infra/backup-volatile-filter.js\"\n\n✅ agent/tmp       → skip\n✅ agent/cache     → skip\n✅ agent/shell_snapshots → skip\n✅ agent/config    → keep\n✅ browser/cache   → skip\n✅ archived        → skip\n✅ lock file       → skip\n✅ journal         → skip\n✅ WAL             → skip\n✅ SHM             → skip\n10/10 passed\n```\n\n### Test suite\n\n```\nnpx vitest run src/infra/backup-volatile-filter.test.ts\n  Test Files 1 passed  Tests 20+ passed\n```\n\n### Formatting & lint\n\n```\npnpm exec oxfmt --check ...  (pass)\nnpx oxlint ...  (clean)\ngit diff --check  (clean)\n```\n\n## Change Type\n\n- [x] Bug fix\n\n## Scope\n\n- [x] Infrastructure (backup archive filter)\n\n## Security Impact\n\n- New permissions? No\n- Secrets handling changed? No\n- New network calls? No",
